{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:KnotsParticlesConfinement.MesonScaleIndependence","@type":"LeanModule","name":"KnotsParticlesConfinement.MesonScaleIndependence","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.meson_scale_independence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.meson_scale_independence","kind":"theorem","line":27,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/meson-scale-independence.lean#L27-L49","doc":"**Meson scale independence (geometric core).**\n\nThe pion mass `m_π` cannot be derived from the substrate parameters\n`(m_e, q_0)` alone. The per-knot mass scale is the product\n`m_e · Vol(K) · ρ(K) / ℏ_q²`; for the meson the binding topology is\nthe Hopf link, whose complement has hyperbolic volume `0`, whereas\nthe baryon's Borromean complement has strictly positive volume. So\nthe geometric invariant that would fix a mass scale from `(m_e, q_0)`\n**vanishes** for the meson — the scale must come from the independent\ncalibration `P_avg^π` (CAL-3).\n\nThe Lean content is exactly this geometric obstruction: the meson\nvolume is `0` while the baryon volume is positive, so the linear\nvolume-scaling map sends the meson's geometric scale to `0`\nindependently of `(m_e, q_0)`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:meson-scale-independence","label":"prop:meson-scale-independence","md":"quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/meson-scale-independence.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.borromeanComplementVolume","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.borromeanComplementVolume","kind":"def","line":23,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/meson-scale-independence.lean#L23-L25","doc":"Hyperbolic volume of the Borromean complement `Vol(𝓑₃) = 8G`\n(`G` = Catalan's constant), the baryon geometric mass scale. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.hopfComplementVolume","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.hopfComplementVolume","kind":"def","line":20,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/meson-scale-independence.lean#L20-L21","doc":"Hyperbolic volume of the Hopf-link complement (a solid torus): `0`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}